OL,3,GNEWSAShock safety failures of Salford's
OL,4,Aunregistered HMOs
OL,5,
OL,6,FNearly every unregistered HMO inspected
OL,7,Fin Salford failed to meet minimum
OL,8,Fsafety standards, a report has found.
OL,10,FSalford City Council investigated 91
OL,11,Fproperties and found more than 1,000
OL,12,F"unacceptable hazards", including 161
OL,13,Fwhich posed a risk to tenants' health
OL,14,Fand well being.
OL,16,FOne home was flagged to the council for
OL,17,Fhaving a single timer-operated boiler,
OL,18,Fwhich left tenants unable to control
OL,19,Ftheir own heating, leading to
OL,20,F"excessive cold". Another landlord was
OL,21,Ffined for lack of heating and fire
OL,22,Frisks.
OL,23,APub: 18-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext PageB NW Eng NewsC Reg TVF Weather
FL,409,400,260,160,0,100
